 ### Refunds
 
-You can refund UPI payments up to 60 days after the original payment. Refunds are asynchronous and can take up to 7 business days to complete. Stripe notifies you of the final refund status using the `refund.updated` or `refund.failed` _webhook_ (A webhook is a real-time push notification sent to your application as a JSON payload through HTTPS requests) event. When a refund succeeds, the [Refund](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/object.md) object’s status transitions to `succeeded`. In the rare instance that a refund fails, the `Refund` object’s status transitions to `failed` and Stripe returns the amount to your balance. You’ll need to arrange an alternative way to refund your customer.
+You can refund UPI payments up to 60 days after the original payment. Refunds are asynchronous and can take up to 7 business days to complete. Stripe notifies you of the final refund status using the `refund.updated` or `refund.failed` *webhook* (A webhook is a real-time push notification sent to your application as a JSON payload through HTTPS requests) event. When a refund succeeds, the [Refund](https://docs.stripe.com/api/refunds/object.md) object’s status transitions to `succeeded`. In the rare instance that a refund fails, the `Refund` object’s status transitions to `failed` and Stripe returns the amount to your balance. You’ll need to arrange an alternative way to refund your customer.
 
